        'WORD FIRST: two remembrances at the head of everything - Yahweh\'s, "yea, they may forget, yet will I not forget thee." (Isaiah 49:15), "I have graven thee upon the palms of my hands" (Isaiah 49:16), "He hath remembered his covenant for ever" (Psalms 105:8), the bow as His own memorial (Genesis 9:15-16); and man\'s, "There is no remembrance of former things" (Ecclesiastes 1:11), "my people have forgotten me days without number" (Jeremiah 2:32).',
