      howToRun: 'Prayer + the anchor (5): open in prayer; read Philippians 1:6 and Luke 13:6-8 aloud (KJV). | Recap last week (8): what process did you draw as a loop, and what is its proof? | His words (5): read Darrell\'s sentences aloud, in order, before any commentary. | Teach the big idea (15): Yahweh finishes (Philippians 1:6; John 17:4; John 19:30); the hand (Isaiah 41:13; Psalms 37:24); the dresser (Luke 13:6-8). | The second touch and the potter (10): Mark 8:22-25; Jeremiah 18:3-4. | Finish, join, and hear (7): Luke 14:28-30; Nehemiah 2:6; Ezekiel 37:17; Exodus 18; Acts 6. | Our own house (8): the monitor held by the hand until 874 of 874. | Hands-on in the app (10): Admin - Systems, then Church - Harvest; each person writes the next touch on one thing they flagged and left. | Discussion (5): use the prompts below. | Send-off (2): read the benefits aloud; close with Psalms 34:8.',
